    {
      "id": "qa_1749025644678_k1ugu3fd",
      "question": "How to get admission for mbbs??",
      "answer": "To get admission for MBBS at KGMU, you must meet the following criteria:\n\n1.  **Eligibility:** You must have passed the 10+2 examination with Physics, Chemistry, Biology/Biotechnology, and English. You must have also obtained a minimum aggregate score as per the regulations.\n2.  **Entrance Exam:** You need to qualify for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET) exam.\n3.  **Application:** You must apply for counselling conducted by the relevant authority (e.g., UP DGME for Uttar Pradesh state quota) after qualifying for NEET.\n4.  **Counselling and Admission:** Based on your NEET rank and the availability of seats, you will be allotted a seat in KGMU during the counselling process. You'll then need to complete the admission formalities.\n\nFor more detailed and up-to-date information, please visit the KGMU website ([www.kgmu.org](http://www.kgmu.org/)) and the official websites of the NEET conducting authorities and the counselling body (UP DGME).\n",
